<title>USA: M-Wave cuts plant workforce by 20 percent.</title>
<headline>M-Wave cuts plant workforce by 20 percent.</headline>
<dateline>BENSENVILLE, Ill. 1997-02-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>M-Wave Inc said Friday it laid off 20 of the 100 workers at its Poly Circuits manufacturing plant and eliminated a second shift to improve efficiency at the facility.</p>
<p>The company, which a spokesman said has a total of 145 employees, said the moves will not reduce production levels.</p>
<p>M-Wave makes microwave printed circuit boards that are used in industrial and military applications.</p>
<p>The company's shares closed down 1/8 Friday at 3-1/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
</text>
